%N A400848 Averages of twin prime pairs that are not 2-dense numbers A174973.
%C A400848 In other words: averages of twin prime pairs whose number of 2-dense sublists of divisors is greater than 1.
%C A400848 Also averages of twin prime pairs (p, q) such that both the symmetric representation of sigma(p) and the symmetric representation of sigma(q) share at least one point.
%H A400848 James C. McMahon, <a href="/A400848/b400848.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400848 102 is in the sequence because it is the average of the twin prime pair (101, 103) and because 102 has two 2-dense sublists of divisors, they are [1, 2, 3, 6] and [17, 34, 51, 102], so 102 is not a 2-dense number.
%e A400848 Also 102 is in the sequence because it is the average of the twin prime pair (101, 103) and both the symmetric representation of sigma(101) and the symmetric representation of sigma(103) share four line segments. The diagrams of both the symmetric representation of sigma(101) and the symmetric representation of sigma(103) are too large to include here.
%t A400848 Select[Prime[Range[743]],PrimeQ[#+2]&&Max[Ratios[Divisors[#+1]]]>2&]+1 (* _James C. McMahon_, Nov 11 2026 *)
%Y A400848 Intersection of A014574 and A238524.
%Y A400848 The union of A401769 and this sequence gives A014574.
